+PASS 11 / V43 "GL Accounts In Bucket" (2026-09-10) -- user reported "I can't
+see GL code in this report" against a real production export. Two real
+things were true at once: (a) the GL-wise account breakdown (GL Account,
+GL Name, GL Total, POS Total, Difference, Status) has been in the Summary
+sheet's "GL-WISE SUMMARY" block since V42.2, but sits to the right of the
+Store-wise table (columns G onward) rather than in its own sheet, so it's
+easy to miss on a quick look; (b) more concretely, the row-level "POS to
+GL" / "GL Matched" / "Exceptions" sheets had "GL Main Account" blank on
+EVERY row, with no other GL account visibility at that grain at all --
+confirmed against the user's real export (786 exception rows, 89 GL Matched
+rows, all blank). (b) is a real, structural gap: bucket matching sums
+possibly-many GL rows against possibly-many POS rows for a Store+Date, so
+there genuinely is no single GL row a given POS row "matched" -- but that's
+a reason "GL Main Account" specifically can't be filled in per row, not a
+reason no GL account information belongs on those rows at all. Added a new
+"GL Accounts In Bucket" column to the row-level sheets and "GL Accounts In
+This Bucket" to Store Date Buckets/Top 20 Exceptions: every GL account
+posted in that Store+Date bucket, each with its own signed SAR total (e.g.
+"11020904 (SAR 200.00), 11020908 (SAR 100.00)"). Purely additive labeling --
+does not read into bucket_status, bucket_diff, tolerance, or any other
+matching decision; reuses the same per-bucket GL-by-account grouping V42
+item 6 already computed for the "Uncovered GL Accounts" column, just
+un-filtered to all accounts instead of only the uncovered subset.
